Task 1: Explain Generative AI
Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) is a type of AI that learns patterns from existing data and uses them to create new content, such as text, images, music, videos, and computer code. Unlike traditional AI, which mainly classifies information or makes predictions, GenAI can generate original outputs based on user prompts.

Two real-world examples are ChatGPT, which generates answers, explanations, and code from text prompts, and DALL·E, which generates images based on written descriptions.
Task 2: GenAI vs. Traditional AI
Aspect	Generative AI (GenAI)	Traditional AI
Main purpose	Creates new content.	Classifies data, predicts outcomes, or makes decisions.
Input	Prompts, text, images, audio, or other data.	Structured data, images, text, or other input features.
Working method	Learns patterns and generates new outputs based on them.	Often learns decision boundaries, rules, or patterns for specific tasks.
Creativity	Can produce varied and novel content.	Usually focuses on predefined prediction or decision tasks.
Output	Text, images, music, video, or code.	Class labels, scores, predictions, or recommendations.
Example	ChatGPT generating a story.	An email spam classifier identifying spam messages.
Conclusion: Generative AI focuses on creating new content, while traditional AI is commonly used for prediction, classification, and decision-making. Some AI systems can perform both kinds of tasks.
